[
  {
    "_comments": [
      "Field display names and form sections for the generated forms (bc-aidp-next-golive#298).",
      "",
      "CodeGen's AI pass names fields and groups them into form sections only for entities and fields it",
      "creates. On a database built from migrations these entities already exist, so CodeGen fell back to",
      "column-derived names ('Organization Type ID') and one 'Details' section. These rows pin the names",
      "and sections next shipped, so the generated forms are reproducible from this repo.",
      "",
      "AutoUpdateDisplayName / AutoUpdateCategory go to false so a later CodeGen run keeps them.",
      "GeneratedFormSection 'Category' puts the field in its Category's section instead of 'Details'.",
      "Section icons come from each entity's FieldCategoryInfo setting (metadata/entity-settings/).",
      "",
      "Primary keys and lookup-name fields (Person, JobFunction, ...) are never drawn, but a field left in",
      "'Details' still produces an empty Details section, so they take their siblings' category.",
      "",
      "Address __mj_Latitude / __mj_Longitude are the geo aliases of Latitude / Longitude, which the",
      "'Geographic Location' section already shows, so they stay off the generated form.",
      "",
      "Dev loop after editing: mj migrate -> mj sync push --dir metadata -> mj codegen."
    ],
